{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-02_cc-ex99_1.htm, sha256 85ce362387efad18753c1ef4bdf4413cc1384cca87aca2ad286852d5c998a877.\nEX-99.1 2 cc-ex99_1.htm EX-99.1\nEXHIBIT 99.1\nThe Chemours Company Reports Third Quarter Results\nWilmington, Del., November 2, 2026 \u2013 The Chemours Company (\u201cChemours\u201d or \u201cthe Company\u201d) (NYSE: CC), a global chemistry company with leading market positions in Thermal & Specialized Solutions (\u201cTSS\u201d), Titanium Technologies (\u201cTT\u201d), and Advanced Performance Materials (\u201cAPM\u201d), today announced its financial results for the third quarter 2026.\nKey Third Quarter 2026 Results & Recent Highlights1\n\u2022 Net Sales of $1.5 billion, up slightly from the prior-year quarter, reflecting an approximately 10% year-over-year pricing increase in TT and 26% year-over-year growth in APM Performance Solutions. \u2022 Net Income attributable to Chemours of $196 million, or $1.29 per diluted share, compared with Net Income attributable to Chemours of $46 million, or $0.31 per diluted share, in the corresponding prior-year quarter. \u2022 Adjusted Net Income2 of $31 million, or $0.21 per diluted share, compared with Adjusted Net Income of $26 million, or $0.17 per diluted share, in the corresponding prior-year quarter. \u2022 Adjusted EBITDA2,3 of $200 million, compared with $189 million in the prior-year quarter, driven by improved pricing in TT and growth in APM Performance Solutions. \u2022 As previously announced, entered into a settlement with the State of North Carolina and 11 local entities to resolve litigation relating to PFAS and other historical discharges from Fayetteville Works, as well as claims of PFAS contamination unrelated to that site, including from the use of AFFF. \u2022 Formally launching Chemours\u2019 liquid cooling portfolio, including four two-phase direct-to-chip and one immersion cooling fluid under the Faizeon\u2122 liquid cooling brand. \u2022 Completed the sale of the Kuan Yin property for total net consideration of ~$340 million, including the remaining land parcel for $56 million of gross proceeds.\n\u201cOur third-quarter results demonstrate strong year-over-year performance in TT and APM, reflecting pricing execution in TiO2 and increased demand across Performance Solutions\u2019 high-value AI infrastructure including data center and semiconductor end markets,\u201d said Denise Dignam, Chemours President and CEO. \u201cWe also continued to make meaningful progress under our Pathway to Thrive, including reaching a settlement with the State of North Carolina, driving operational improvements through the Chemours Business System, and closing the sale of the final parcel of land associated with our former Kuan Yin property. While we continue to navigate TSS stationary aftermarket dynamics and a softer macroeconomic environment, we remain focused on disciplined execution of our strategic priorities and the factors within our control to drive long-term returns for shareholders.\u201d\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "1 Certain prior period amounts have been revised to correct for certain immaterial errors as further described in our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2025 as well as the 2025 Earnings Presentation.\n2 Non-GAAP measures, including Adjusted Net Income, Adjusted EPS and Adjusted EBITDA referred to throughout, principally exclude the impact of recent litigation settlements for legacy environmental matters and associated fees, in addition to other unallocated items \u2013 please refer to the attached \"Reconciliation of GAAP Financial Measures to Non-GAAP Financial Measures (Unaudited)\u201d.\n3 Adjusted EBITDA excludes net income attributable to noncontrolling interests, net interest expense, depreciation and amortization, and all remaining provision for income taxes from Adjusted Net Income. See the corresponding reconciliation referenced in footnote #2.\n4 Restricted cash approximated $103 million of the end of the third quarter of 2026, reflected primarily the PFAS Insurance Escrow and will be further described in our Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q for the quarter ended September 30, 2026.\nEXHIBIT 99.1\nTotal Chemours\nQ3 2026\nQ3 2025\nY-o-Y % \u2206\nQ2 2026\nQ-o-Q % \u2206\nNet Sales (millions)\n$1,540\n$1,495\n3%\n$1,591\n(3%)\nNet Income (Loss) attributable to Chemours (millions)\n$196\n$46\n326%\n($274)\n172%\nEarnings (Loss) Per Share2\n$1.29\n$0.31\n316%\n($1.81)\n171%\nAdjusted Net Income\n$31\n$26\n19%\n$64\n(52%)\nAdjusted EPS\n$0.21\n$0.17\n24%\n$0.42\n(50%)\nAdjusted EBITDA (millions)\n$200\n$189\n6%\n$247\n(19%)\nThird quarter 2026 Net Sales were approximately $1.5 billion, an increase of approximately 3% compared with the prior-year quarter. The year-over-year increase in Net Sales was driven by a 5% increase in pricing, partially offset by a 2% decrease in volumes and a slight currency headwind. The pricing increase was primarily driven by previously announced price actions in TT, complemented by a favorable mix shift toward APM Performance Solutions. Lower year-over-year volumes primarily reflected anticipated lower North American stationary AC aftermarket sales of TSS OpteonTM blends compared with elevated demand in the prior-year quarter.\nThird quarter 2026 Net Income attributable to Chemours was $196 million, or $1.29 per diluted share, compared with $46 million, or $0.31 per diluted share, in the prior-year quarter. Current-year third-quarter Net Income included the receipt of $150 million related to the PFAS insurance proceeds MOU that was executed in connection with the finalization of the judicial consent order (\"JCO\") with the State of New Jersey. This was presented as a reduction to Selling, general, and administrative expense. Third quarter Adjusted Net Income increased 19% compared with the prior-year quarter, aligned with trends in Adjusted EBITDA as highlighted below.\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "Adjusted EBITDA for the third quarter of 2026 was $200 million, compared with $189 million in the prior-year quarter. The increase was driven by pricing momentum in TT and a favorable mix shift toward APM Performance Solutions, partially offset by lower TSS volumes associated with the North American stationary AC aftermarket dynamics noted above and higher costs across each business.\n2 On a diluted earnings per share basis.\nEXHIBIT 99.1\nThermal & Specialized Solutions\nQ3 2026\nQ3 2025\nY-o-Y % \u2206\nQ2 2026\nQ-o-Q % \u2206\nNet Sales (millions)\n$510\n$560\n(9%)\n$591\n(14%)\nOpteon\u2122 Refrigerants\n$287\n$368\n(22%)\n$337\n(15%)\nFreon\u2122 Refrigerants\n$100\n$94\n6%\n$150\n(33%)\nFoam, Propellants & Other (FP&O)\n$123\n$98\n26%\n$104\n18%\nAdjusted EBITDA (millions)\n$136\n$194\n(30%)\n$213\n(36%)\nAdjusted EBITDA Margin\n27%\n35%\n(8) ppts\n36%\n(9) ppts\nTSS segment third quarter 2026 Net Sales were $510 million, a decrease of 9% compared with the prior-year quarter, driven by a 9% decrease in volumes and a slight decrease in price.\nThe decrease in volumes was primarily attributable to lower North American stationary AC aftermarket sales of TSS Opteon\u2122 blends compared with elevated demand in the prior-year quarter, which benefited from the initial aftermarket channel fill associated with the stationary AC technology transition under the U.S. AIM Act.\nAdjusted EBITDA for the quarter decreased 30% to $136 million, while Adjusted EBITDA Margin decreased eight points to 27%. The decrease in Adjusted EBITDA was primarily driven by the lower OpteonTM stationary aftermarket sales noted above and higher costs incurred during the period.\nSequentially, TSS Net Sales decreased 14%, driven by lower volumes associated with seasonal demand trends in the North American stationary AC aftermarket, as well as a slight currency headwind, partially offset by pricing.\nTitanium Technologies\nQ3 2026\nQ3 2025\nY-o-Y % \u2206\nQ2 2026\nQ-o-Q % \u2206\nNet Sales (millions)\n$680\n$612\n11%\n$661\n3%\nTiO2 Pigment\n$650\n$591\n10%\n$639\n2%\nMinerals\n$30\n$21\n43%\n$22\n36%\nAdjusted EBITDA (millions)\n$85\n$25\n240%\n$48\n77%\nAdjusted EBITDA Margin\n13%\n4%\n9 ppts\n7%\n6 ppts\nTT segment third quarter 2026 Net Sales were $680 million, an 11% increase compared with the prior-year quarter. The increase was driven by a 10% increase in global pricing and a 1% increase in global volumes, partially offset by a slight currency headwind. Pricing increased across all regions in connection with recent pricing announcements, while global volume growth reflected strength in North America, Latin America, and APAC excluding China that more than offset lower volumes across EMEA and China.\nTT segment third quarter 2026 Adjusted EBITDA increased to $85 million from $25 million in the prior-year quarter and Adjusted EBITDA Margin increased by nine points to 13%. The increase in Adjusted EBITDA was primarily driven by the global pricing strength noted above and higher volumes, partially offset by modest cost inflation.\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "Sequentially, TT segment third quarter 2026 Net Sales increased 3%, driven by a 4% increase in price, reflecting continued execution of recent TiO2 pricing announcements, partially offset by a 1% decrease in global volumes and a slight currency headwind.\n2 On a diluted earnings per share basis.\nEXHIBIT 99.1\nAdvanced Performance Materials\nQ3 2026\nQ3 2025\nY-o-Y % \u2206\nQ2 2026\nQ-o-Q % \u2206\nNet Sales (millions)\n$337\n$311\n8%\n$326\n3%\nAdvanced Materials\n$184\n$190\n(3%)\n$184\n0%\nPerformance Solutions\n$153\n$121\n26%\n$142\n8%\nAdjusted EBITDA (millions)\n$24\n$14\n71%\n$26\n(8%)\nAdjusted EBITDA Margin\n7%\n5%\n2 ppts\n8%\n(1) ppts\nAPM segment third quarter 2026 Net Sales were $337 million, an 8% increase compared with the prior-year quarter. The increase was driven by a 6% increase in price and a 2% increase in volume, partially offset by a slight currency headwind. Performance Solutions Net Sales increased 26%, reflecting continued order book strength and momentum in high-value specialty products serving data center and semiconductor end markets.\nAPM segment third quarter 2026 Adjusted EBITDA increased 71% to $24 million compared with the prior-year quarter, while Adjusted EBITDA Margin increased two points to 7%. The increase in Adjusted EBITDA was primarily driven by a favorable mix shift toward higher-value Performance Solutions products serving data center and semiconductor end markets, partially offset by higher costs incurred during the period.\nSequentially, APM segment third quarter 2026 Net Sales increased approximately 3%, driven by a 2% increase in price and a 1% increase in volume. Performance Solutions Net Sales increased 8%, reflecting continued order book strength and momentum in high-value specialty products serving data center and semiconductor end markets.\nEXHIBIT 99.1\nOther Non-Reportable Segment\nThe Performance Chemicals and Intermediates business in the Company\u2019s Other Non-Reportable Segment had Net Sales and Adjusted EBITDA for the third quarter 2026 of $13 million and $1 million, respectively.\nCorporate Expenses\nCorporate Expenses were $46 million in the third quarter of 2026, an increase of approximately $1 million compared with the prior-year quarter.\nLiquidity and Capital Allocation\nAs of September 30, 2026, consolidated gross debt was $3.9 billion. Debt, net of $698 million in unrestricted4 cash and cash equivalents, was $3.2 billion, resulting in a Net Leverage ratio of approximately 4.3x on a trailing twelve-month Adjusted EBITDA basis. Total liquidity was $1.7 billion, composed of $698 million in unrestricted cash and cash equivalents and $953 million of revolving credit facility capacity, net of outstanding letters of credit.\n"}
{"page": 5, "text": "Operating cash flows for the third quarter of 2026 were $149 million, which includes the aforementioned receipt of $150 million in restricted cash related to the PFAS insurance proceeds MOU in connection with the finalization of the JCO with the State of New Jersey, partially offset by an approximately $100 million use of restricted cash to fund settlement payments associated with the 2025 settlement with the State of New Jersey and approximately $25 million of taxes related to the property sale in Kuan Yin. This is compared with $146 million of operating cash flows in the prior-year quarter.\nCapital expenditures for the third quarter of 2026 amounted to $51 million, an increase compared with $41 million in the prior-year quarter.\nFree Cash Flows for the third quarter of 2026 were $98 million, compared with $105 million in the third quarter of 2025.\n3 Restricted cash was $103 million at the end of the third quarter of 2026, primarily reflecting PFAS Insurance proceeds MOU escrow recorded during the quarter as further described in our Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q for the quarter ended September 30, 2026.\nEXHIBIT 99.1\nFourth Quarter 2026 Outlook\nIn the fourth quarter, the Company expects consolidated Net Sales to decrease in the range of 5% to 10%, sequentially, driven by seasonality in TSS and TT, with consolidated Adjusted EBITDA expected to range between $160 million and $185 million. Corporate Expenses are expected to be approximately $40 million to $45 million. The Company also anticipates capital expenditures to be between $75 million and $85 million, with positive Free Cash Flows.\nTSS expects Net Sales will sequentially decrease in the high-teens to low-twenties percentage range, driven by traditional seasonal patterns related to the North American cooling season. Adjusted EBITDA is expected to be between $105 million and $115 million.\nTT expects a sequential Net Sales decrease in the high single-digit to low-teens percentage range, driven by seasonality. Adjusted EBITDA is expected to range between $60 million and $65 million.\nAPM expects a sequential Net Sales increase in the low-to-mid teens percentage range, driven by order book strength for Performance Solutions products and certain customer contractual obligations benefiting the fourth quarter. Adjusted EBITDA for APM is expected to be between $40 million and $45 million.\nFull Year 2026 Outlook\n"}
{"page": 6, "text": "The Company expects 2026 Net Sales to grow approximately 2% over 2025, with Adjusted EBITDA between $775 million and $800 million. Capital expenditures are anticipated to be between $220 million and $230 million, with overall Free Cash Flow Conversion above 15%, which includes receipt of $150 million in restricted cash related to the PFAS insurance proceeds MOU in connection with the finalization of the JCO with the State of New Jersey, partially offset by legal settlement payments in the year related to the finalization of the JCO with the State of New Jersey and the announced settlement with the State of North Carolina during the third quarter of 2026 as well as the taxes associated with the Kuan Yin property sale now complete. The Company now anticipates achieving a Net Leverage ratio below 4.2x in 2026.\nEXHIBIT 99.1\nConference Call\nAs previously announced, Chemours will hold a conference call and webcast on November 3, 2026, at 8:00 a.m. Eastern Standard Time. The webcast and materials can be accessed by visiting the Events & Presentations page of Chemours\u2019 investor website, investors.chemours.com. A webcast replay of the conference call will be available on Chemours\u2019 investor website.\nAbout The Chemours Company\nThe Chemours Company (NYSE: CC) is a global leader in providing industrial and specialty chemical products for markets, including coatings, plastics, refrigeration and air conditioning, transportation, semiconductor and advanced electronics, general industrial, and oil and gas. Through our three businesses \u2013 Thermal & Specialized Solutions, Titanium Technologies, and Advanced Performance Materials \u2013 we deliver application expertise and chemistry-based innovations that solve customers\u2019 biggest challenges. Our flagship products are sold under prominent brands such as Opteon\u2122, Freon\u2122, Ti-Pure\u2122, Nafion\u2122, Teflon\u2122, Viton\u2122, and Krytox\u2122. Headquartered in Wilmington, Delaware, and listed on the NYSE under the symbol CC, Chemours has approximately 5,700 employees and 28 manufacturing sites and serves approximately 2,400 customers in approximately 110 countries. For more information, visit chemours.com or follow us on LinkedIn.\nNon-GAAP Financial Measures\n"}
{"page": 7, "text": "We prepare our financial statements in accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). Within this press release, we may make reference to Adjusted Net Income, Adjusted EPS, Adjusted EBITDA, Free Cash Flows, Free Cash Flow Conversion, Total Debt Principal, Net and Net Leverage Ratio which are non-GAAP financial measures. The Company includes these non-GAAP financial measures because management believes they are useful to investors in that they provide for greater transparency with respect to supplemental information used by management in its financial and operational decision making. Management uses Adjusted Net Income, Adjusted EPS and Adjusted EBITDA, which adjust for (i) certain non-cash items, (ii) certain items we believe are not indicative of ongoing operating performance, or (iii) certain nonrecurring, unusual or infrequent items to evaluate the Company's performance in order to have comparable financial results to analyze changes in our underlying business from period to period. Additionally, Free Cash Flows, Free Cash Flow Conversion, Total Debt Principal, Net and Net Leverage Ratio are utilized as liquidity measures to assess the cash generation of our businesses and ongoing liquidity position.\nAccordingly, the Company believes the presentation of these non-GAAP financial measures, when used in conjunction with GAAP financial measures, is a useful financial analysis tool that can assist investors in assessing the Company's operating performance and underlying prospects. This analysis should not be considered in isolation or as a substitute for analysis of our results as reported under GAAP. This analysis, as well as the other information in this press release, should be read in conjunction with the Company's financial statements and footnotes contained in the documents that the Company files with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. The non-GAAP financial measures used by the Company in this press release may be different from the methods used by other companies. The Company does not provide a reconciliation of certain forward-looking non-GAAP financial measures to the most directly comparable GAAP reported financial measures on a forward-looking basis because it is unable to predict with reasonable certainty the ultimate outcome of unusual gains and losses, potential future asset impairments and pending litigation without unreasonable effort. These items are uncertain, depend on various factors, and could have a material impact on GAAP reported results for the guidance period. For more information on the non-GAAP financial measures, please refer to the attached schedules or the table, \"Reconciliation of GAAP Financial Measures to Non-GAAP Financial Measures (Unaudited)\" and materials posted to the Company's website at investors.chemours.com.\nEXHIBIT 99.1\nForward-Looking Statements\n"}
